# The TEI P5 release that `opm odd document` documents, and that TEI-targeting
# ODDs are merged onto. One release number, as it appears in TEIC/TEI's own tag
# `P5_Release_<version>`.
#
# TEI ships on its own schedule, and a new release can change content models
# and prose. Moving to one is therefore a decision, taken in a reviewed commit:
# bump the line below, then run the "TEI data" workflow, which builds
# p5all.xml from exactly this tag and publishes it to the rolling `tei-data`
# release. Nothing else republishes it — no schedule, no discovery of newer
# tags — so the data moves only when someone decides it should.
#
# See CONTRIBUTING.md, "Updating the TEI data".
4.12.0
